{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And they sent the coat of many colors and brought it to their father</b> — by command, or the meaning is 'and they brought' — the messengers who bring it, for they were still in Dothan, and they said, 'This we found; recognize now, please.' Or they sent it to Hebron, to the house of one of them, and when they arrived they brought it in before their father and said to him, 'This we found.' And all this was to act as strangers concerning the matter, for if they had remained silent he would have suspected them, saying, 'You killed him,' for he knew their jealousy toward him. And some interpret 'וַיְשַׁלְּחוּ' — that they thrust arrows (שֶׁלַח) into it to tear it in many places in the likeness of animal bites, from the language of 'בְּשֶׁלַח יַעֲבֹרוּ' (Job 36:12). And the reason it says 'the coat of stripes (הַפַּסִּים)' is that they sent it so that he would recognize it by the stripes (פַּסִּים) which he had made for him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:21.298820079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}